ana: Heads-up — onboarding sampleapp surfaced a noisy SDK parity issue for embeddings + rerank. Short summary below.

ben: TL;DR?

ana: (typo) sorry. TL;DR: Node helper occasionally returns the wrong shape for single-item batches and rerank responses use inconsistent score keys across model rollouts. Also saw duplicate side-effects when auth retry replays without preserving idempotency header.

chi: Can you paste a tiny repro and an example response?

ana: Yep — pared down: 
```
// Node (sampleapp helper)
const batch = batcher.make([{text: 'lookup'}]);
// -> [ [0.1, 0.02, ...] ]  // nested array for n=1

// Python
b = batcher.make(['lookup'])
# -> [0.1, 0.02, ...]  // flat vector

// Rerank examples we've seen from hosted variants:
{ "results": [{ "id": "doc1", "score": 0.91 }] }
{ "results": [{ "id": "doc1", "ranking_score": 0.91 }] }
{ "results": [{ "id": "doc1", "score_value": 0.91 }] }
```

rahul: I also traced an auth retry: token refresh -> replay -> request sent without x-rw-idempotency-token -> server processes twice for side-effecting endpoints.

ben: Re: shape — helper is ambiguous about its contract. Quick fix: always return array-of-vectors (list-of-list) at the helper boundary so retrievers can assume [N][D]. I'll open a tiny PR with unit tests for n=1 and n>1.

chi: For rerank keys we should add a compatibility layer in the SDK that normalizes to `score`. Fallback order: score > ranking_score > score_value > confidence. Prevents breakage when a model canary renames the key. I can push a patch.

ana: Short-term workaround I added to the sampleapp template to unblock new users: normalize embedding shape + normalize rerank score before downstream logic. Snippet: 
```js
let emb = resp.data;
if (!Array.isArray(emb[0])) emb = [emb];
const mapped = res.results.map(r => ({ id: r.id, score: r.score ?? r.ranking_score ?? r.score_value ?? r.confidence }));
```

ci-bot: Created ticket DEVEX-4220: "SDK parity: embedding batch shape + rerank key variance + auth retry idempotency". Linked PRs requested: node-batcher-clarify, sdk-rerank-normalize, auth-retry-preserve-id. Please add an e2e parity test in sampleapp that runs Node & Py flows against a fixed fixture and asserts identical normalized outputs.

auth-bot: Recommendation: preserve x-rw-idempotency-token across auth retries by default. Will open infra patch and an integration test ensuring dedupe.

ben: I'll land the node helper PR with tests and a docstring: "returns array-of-vectors: [[v1],[v2],...]". chi, please add CI schema checks for rerank responses so future renames fail fast.

chi: On it. I'll also add an SDK regression test that asserts `score` exists for each rerank result after mapping.

ana: Thanks all — once PRs land we'll remove the temporary shim and update onboarding docs to note the expected helper contract and the rerank normalization. Will link logs to DEVEX-4220. :rocket:
